 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The eviction policy is 2Q. The worker maintains two queues: an in-memory first-use queue (A1) for items seen once, and a main queue (A2) for items seen at least twice. New entries enter A1; on a hit, entries move from A1 to A2. Eviction removes from A1 first, then A2, protecting reused comparison sheets from one-off screening scans. The queue size split is configurable and remains private to the preview worker. This choice adds bookkeeping for two queues and a promotion path, but preserves the external interface, queue concurrency limits, and 12 GiB disk budget.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q with A1/A2 queues and promotion on second access | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | LRU has low bookkeeping but evicts useful comparison sheets during long sequential screenings. Frequency with aging retains popular clips but adds counter maintenance and can retain yesterday's favorites too long after project switches. 2Q protects reused sheets from one-off scans with extra bookkeeping confined to the preview worker, matching the requirement to protect comparison sheets during big screenings. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Eviction policy selected as 2Q per user direction after evaluation of LRU and aged frequency.
+
+### Deferred
+1. Exact A1/A2 size split and promotion thresholds to be tuned during pilot load testing.
